## PHASE 2 — Project links

Every launch can carry links. All optional.

**Fields in the create flow**, grouped under a "Links" heading:

| Field | Prefix shown | Validation |
|---|---|---|
| Website | `https://` | Valid URL, https only |
| X | `x.com/` | Handle characters only |
| Telegram | `t.me/` | Handle, `+invite`, or `joinchat/…` |

Store them in the token's metadata JSON alongside name, description and image,
so they live on IPFS with everything else and are readable by anyone without
our interface.

**Display:**

- Token page: a links row beneath the project name — small icons with the
  handle beside each, rendering only links that exist. No empty slots, no
  greyed placeholders.
- Discover cards: icons only, no handles, and only if at least one exists.
- All links `target="_blank"` with `rel="noopener noreferrer"`.
- Inline SVG icons in our palette. Do not use platform brand colours, and do
  not add an icon library for four glyphs.

**One thing that must not be blurred.** These links are typed in by the project
and are not verified. We never built link verification, and displaying an X
handle a project entered is not proof they control it.

So: never label this section "Verified links" and never place a check mark
beside it. Call it "Links" and add a small faint line: *"Provided by the
project. Not verified by BALLAST."*

That distinction matters more here than almost anywhere else on the site,
because "verified" is a word we use precisely — the backing panel earns it, and
this doesn't.

If a link is malformed or a field is empty, store nothing rather than an empty
string, so a dead `t.me/` can never render.

