## PHASE 3 — Discover stats row

Four cards above the tabs. Structure from Uniswap; content is ours.

| Card | Source |
|---|---|
| **Total ballast** | Chain, via BackingLens — sum of verified treasury USD |
| **Tokens launched** | Chain, factory registry union — all time |
| **24h volume** | GeckoTerminal, summed across our pools |
| **Holders** | Blockscout, unique addresses across our tokens |

**Total ballast goes first.** Uniswap leads with token count because volume is
their story. Ours is backing, and nobody else can show it.

Rules that matter more than the layout:

- These must reconcile exactly with what Discover lists beneath them. Same
  source, no separate counters, no cached totals that can drift.
- Each card states its source and freshness in small faint text — "on-chain",
  "GeckoTerminal · 40s ago".
- If a source is unreachable, that card shows an em dash and "unavailable",
  never a zero.
- **Numbers will be small.** Total ballast may read $0. Show it anyway. A stats
  row that only appears once the figures look good is a stats row nobody can
  trust.
- Never animate a value counting up. Crossfade when it changes.

Skeleton loaders while reads resolve, matching final card dimensions exactly.

